<gpx version="1.1" creator="Spokane River Boating Zones map" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
<metadata><name>Spokane River Boating Zones</name><desc>Post Falls Dam to Lake Coeur d'Alene · Kootenai County, Idaho · Current rules: no wake within 100 ft · no towing within 150 ft · surf guideline 200 ft (from shore and docks) · lanes 3,000 ft. No towing anywhere from 1 h after sunset to 1 h before sunrise (Idaho Code § 67-7024(1)–(3), (6)). Draft for review — not yet adopted · map draft 1 · rules as of 2026-10-18 · built 2026-10-19 · depths at summer full pool (2,128 ft). Screening map, not a navigation chart or legal determination. Posted buoys, signs and officers govern. A dock, boom or swim float missing from our data still counts — keep 100 ft (no wake) and 150 ft (no towing). Rules about swimmers, divers and moving boats can't be mapped — keep the required distance from anyone you see. Setbacks are measured from the summer full-pool shoreline; the law measures from today's waterline, so at low water the lines sit further out. Zone boundaries are approximate (not yet surveyed). Made by Cole Van Hersett for Hayden Lake Watershed Improvement District (HLWID) review.</desc><link href="https://colevh2112.github.io/spokane-river-boating/"><text>Interactive map</text></link><time>2026-10-19T12:00:00Z</time><keywords>Spokane River, boating zones, official, draft 1, Draft for review — not yet adopted</keywords></metadata>
<wpt lat="47.70887" lon="-116.9537"><name>PF Dam North</name><cmt>Post Falls Dam — North Channel (Avista)</cmt><desc>Dam / restricted area — No entry between the dam and the boater safety cable at any time (KCC 6.2.123). Equipment can start without warning.</desc><sym>Dam</sym><type>Dam / restricted area</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70398" lon="-116.95583"><name>PF Dam South</name><cmt>Post Falls Dam — South Channel (Avista)</cmt><desc>Dam / restricted area — No entry between the dam and the safety boom at any time (KCC 6.2.123).</desc><sym>Dam</sym><type>Dam / restricted area</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.7045" lon="-116.94878"><name>Spokane St Br</name><cmt>Spokane Street Bridge (Post Falls)</cmt><desc>Bridge — Closure signs on the bridge mark the seasonal No Entry zone downstream of it. Vertical clearance not verified.</desc><sym>Bridge</sym><type>Bridge</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70351" lon="-116.9531"><name>Qemiln Launch</name><cmt>Q'emiln Park boat launch (City of Post Falls)</cmt><desc>Boat launch — Two-lane ramp below the Spokane Street Bridge; opens with Avista summer operations (mid/late June). Idle under the bridge to reach the river. Fees and hours: check the City of Post Falls.</desc><sym>Boat Ramp</sym><type>Boat launch</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70306" lon="-116.95089"><name>Qemiln Park</name><cmt>Q'emiln Park</cmt><desc>Park / beach — City park with swim beach — swimmers likely in summer.</desc><sym>Park</sym><type>Park / beach</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70232" lon="-116.95046"><name>Qemiln WC</name><cmt>Q'emiln Park restrooms</cmt><desc>Restroom / pump-out — Restrooms near the launch.</desc><sym>Restroom</sym><type>Restroom / pump-out</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70607" lon="-116.95072"><name>PF Landing</name><cmt>Post Falls Landing marina (River's Edge)</cmt><desc>Marina / slips — Slips and docks — structures for the setback rules.</desc><sym>Marina</sym><type>Marina / slips</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70911" lon="-116.95283"><name>Falls Park</name><cmt>Falls Park (City of Post Falls / Avista)</cmt><desc>Park / beach — Shore park by the dam (below the reach).</desc><sym>Park</sym><type>Park / beach</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.7021" lon="-116.94286"><name>Templins Fuel</name><cmt>Templin's fuel dock</cmt><desc>Fuel dock — Reported as the only fuel on the reach. Hours not verified.</desc><sym>Gas Station</sym><type>Fuel dock</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.7021" lon="-116.94286"><name>Templins Pump</name><cmt>Templin's pump-out (private)</cmt><desc>Restroom / pump-out — Pump-out reported at the marina; confirm availability.</desc><sym>Restroom</sym><type>Restroom / pump-out</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.7023" lon="-116.94233"><name>Fun Unlimited</name><cmt>Fun Unlimited Post Falls (rentals)</cmt><desc>Rentals / dining / services — Boat and PWC rentals (verify season and hours).</desc><sym>Information</sym><type>Rentals / dining / services</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70273" lon="-116.9426"><name>Templins Grill</name><cmt>Red Lion Templin's restaurant &amp; marina grill</cmt><desc>Rentals / dining / services — Boat-in dining at the marina.</desc><sym>Information</sym><type>Rentals / dining / services</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70278" lon="-116.92697"><name>Black Bay Park</name><cmt>Black Bay Park (City of Post Falls)</cmt><desc>Park / beach — Shore access only — Black Bay itself is a no-motor zone (KCC 6.2.122).</desc><sym>Park</sym><type>Park / beach</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70381" lon="-116.92759"><name>BlackBay Rock</name><cmt>Rock outcrop at the head of Black Bay</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Mapped rock outcrop (OpenStreetMap). Inside the no-motor zone.</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69225" lon="-116.91909"><name>Greensferry</name><cmt>Greensferry boat launch (Kootenai County)</cmt><desc>Boat launch — County launch on the south bank, inside Greensferry Bay; closed 10 p.m.–5 a.m. At the county dock: moor no more than 48 h in any 72, no rafting, quiet hours 10 p.m.–8 a.m. (KCC 6.2.122(B)). Surface and fees reported, not verified — check before bringing a heavy wakeboat.</desc><sym>Boat Ramp</sym><type>Boat launch</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69641" lon="-116.9156"><name>Ferry Br Site</name><cmt>Green's Ferry bridge site (demolished)</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — A bridge once crossed here; old pilings may remain below the surface. Unverified.</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69763" lon="-116.90726"><name>Beach S bank</name><cmt>Informal beach (south bank)</cmt><desc>Beach (people in the water) — Informal beach — people may be in the water.</desc><sym>Swimming Area</sym><type>Beach (people in the water)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69578" lon="-116.89264"><name>Ross Pt Camp</name><cmt>Ross Point Camp &amp; Conference Center waterfront</cmt><desc>Beach (people in the water) — Private camp waterfront — swimmers and paddlers likely in summer.</desc><sym>Swimming Area</sym><type>Beach (people in the water)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69564" lon="-116.88953"><name>Kiwanis Beach</name><cmt>Kiwanis Park swim beach (City of Post Falls)</cmt><desc>Beach (people in the water) — Unguarded city swim beach — swimmers in summer; no wake within 100 ft of people in the water.</desc><sym>Swimming Area</sym><type>Beach (people in the water)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69444" lon="-116.87277"><name>Harbor Is Br</name><cmt>West Harbor Drive bridge (Harbor Island back channel)</cmt><desc>Bridge — Low bridge over the back channel; vertical clearance not verified.</desc><sym>Bridge</sym><type>Bridge</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70029" lon="-116.84432"><name>Mill Rvr Dock</name><cmt>Johnson Mill River Park day-use dock (City of Coeur d'Alene)</cmt><desc>Public / courtesy dock — City day-use dock: no mooring 10 p.m.–6 a.m. or more than 6 hours in any 12; no swimming or wading within 100 ft of the dock (Coeur d'Alene Code §§ 4.20.050–.060).</desc><sym>Marina</sym><type>Public / courtesy dock</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70039" lon="-116.84446"><name>Mill River Bch</name><cmt>Johnson Mill River Park swim beach</cmt><desc>Beach (people in the water) — Swim beach — swimmers likely in summer.</desc><sym>Swimming Area</sym><type>Beach (people in the water)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69559" lon="-116.8165"><name>Atlas Park</name><cmt>Atlas Mill Park / Atlas Waterfront (City of Coeur d'Alene)</cmt><desc>Park / beach — Waterfront park with paddle access.</desc><sym>Park</sym><type>Park / beach</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69648" lon="-116.81877"><name>Atlas Kayak</name><cmt>Atlas Mill Park ADA kayak launch</cmt><desc>Public / courtesy dock — Floating paddle launch — paddlers on the water.</desc><sym>Marina</sym><type>Public / courtesy dock</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69472" lon="-116.81528"><name>USGS 12417650</name><cmt>USGS 12417650 Spokane River below Blackwell</cmt><desc>River / lake gauge — The only stream gauge inside the reach (flow and stage). Live readings on the page header.</desc><sym>Information</sym><type>River / lake gauge</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.68627" lon="-116.80538"><name>BLM Blackwell</name><cmt>Blackwell Island boat launch (BLM)</cmt><desc>Boat launch — Inside the lake-approach no-wake zone. The Blackwell Island Canal upstream is no-motor except from 50 ft above this launch down to the river (KCC 6.2.122(A)(2)(d)). Shallow flats off the ramp at low water.</desc><sym>Boat Ramp</sym><type>Boat launch</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.68665" lon="-116.80524"><name>BLM Flats</name><cmt>Shallow flats off the Blackwell Island launch</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Shallow at fall/winter levels (2004 contours).</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.68605" lon="-116.79936"><name>US-95 Bridge</name><cmt>US-95 bridge over the Spokane River</cmt><desc>Bridge — No-wake from the lake to 300 ft downstream of this bridge (KCC 6.2.122(A)(1)(a)). ITD posts signs and buoys showing where to pass under during work.</desc><sym>Bridge</sym><type>Bridge</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.68131" lon="-116.80652"><name>Slough Bridge</name><cmt>US-95 bridge over Blackwell Slough</cmt><desc>Bridge — Upstream end of the Blackwell Island Canal no-motor zone.</desc><sym>Bridge</sym><type>Bridge</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.68003" lon="-116.80577"><name>Hagadone Ramp</name><cmt>Hagadone Marine boat ramp (Blackwell Slough)</cmt><desc>Boat launch — Private/marina ramp in the slough — no-motor rules apply in the canal (KCC 6.2.122(A)(2)(d)).</desc><sym>Boat Ramp</sym><type>Boat launch</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.67891" lon="-116.80619"><name>Blackwell Mrna</name><cmt>Blackwell Island Marina (Hagadone Marine Group)</cmt><desc>Marina / slips — Marina in the Blackwell Island Canal by the lake. Powerboats reach the lake from here, not the river — the canal north of the US-95 bridge is no-motor (KCC 6.2.122(A)(2)(d)).</desc><sym>Marina</sym><type>Marina / slips</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.67891" lon="-116.80619"><name>Blackwell Fuel</name><cmt>Blackwell Island Marina fuel dock</cmt><desc>Fuel dock — Fuel reported at the marina (verify).</desc><sym>Gas Station</sym><type>Fuel dock</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.67592" lon="-116.80467"><name>Cedars</name><cmt>Cedars Floating Restaurant</cmt><desc>Rentals / dining / services — Boat-in dining at the lake end of the slough.</desc><sym>Information</sym><type>Rentals / dining / services</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.67543" lon="-116.80198"><name>NIC Beach</name><cmt>North Idaho College beach</cmt><desc>Beach (people in the water) — Busy swim beach at the river mouth — inside the lake-approach no-wake zone.</desc><sym>Swimming Area</sym><type>Beach (people in the water)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70168" lon="-116.93085"><name>Shoal Blk Bay</name><cmt>Shallow spot west of Black Bay</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Under ~5 ft at full pool in the 2004 contours — shallower at fall/winter levels. Screening only; not field-checked.</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69795" lon="-116.90863"><name>Shoal S Bank</name><cmt>Shallow spot off the south bank</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Under ~5 ft at full pool in the 2004 contours — shallower at fall/winter levels. Screening only; not field-checked.</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69694" lon="-116.89858"><name>Shoal Ross Pt</name><cmt>Shallow spot opposite Ross Point</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Under ~5 ft at full pool in the 2004 contours — shallower at fall/winter levels. Screening only; not field-checked.</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69497" lon="-116.87685"><name>Shoal Harbor W</name><cmt>Shallow shelf off the south bank west of Harbor Island</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Water under ~5 ft reaches about 50 m out from the south bank here (2004 contours, full pool). Shallower at fall/winter levels.</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69675" lon="-116.87453"><name>Shoal Harbor N</name><cmt>Shallow bar off Harbor Island's northwest shore</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Two small under-5-ft spots in 5–10 ft water near the island (2004 contours). Shallower at fall/winter levels.</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69739" lon="-116.82314"><name>Shoal Atlas</name><cmt>Shallow spot and possible old pilings off the Atlas waterfront</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — One tiny under-5-ft spot in a 15-ft pool (2004 contours). Old log pilings, some submerged, are reported from Cedars to the dam (CdA Press, 2010).</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69163" lon="-116.81063"><name>Bellerive Flat</name><cmt>Shallow flat off Bellerive</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Shallow flat about 36 m off the north bank — depths under 10 ft for 70 m around. Boats have hit old pilings in this narrow stretch (CdA Press, 2010).</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70268" lon="-116.92714"><name>Black Bay</name><cmt>Black Bay</cmt><desc>Landmark — Place name for orientation.</desc><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Landmark</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.6952" lon="-116.871"><name>Harbor Island</name><cmt>Harbor Island</cmt><desc>Landmark — Place name for orientation.</desc><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Landmark</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.6825" lon="-116.803"><name>Blackwell Is</name><cmt>Blackwell Island</cmt><desc>Landmark — Place name for orientation.</desc><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Landmark</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70305" lon="-116.94391"><name>Templins</name><cmt>Templin's</cmt><desc>Landmark — Place name for orientation.</desc><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Landmark</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.70009" lon="-116.8725"><name>BLM Ross Point</name><cmt>Ross Point Day Use Site (BLM)</cmt><desc>Park / beach — BLM day-use site on the north bank: roped swim area and a floating dock for fishing and non-motorized craft. Swimmers and paddlers likely in summer.</desc><sym>Park</sym><type>Park / beach</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69578" lon="-116.89264"><name>Ross Point</name><cmt>Ross Point</cmt><desc>Landmark — Place name for orientation (Ross Point Camp waterfront).</desc><sym>Flag, Blue</sym><type>Landmark</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.69525" lon="-116.91998"><name>Greensferry 2</name><cmt>Shallow bar in Greensferry Bay</cmt><desc>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag) — Mid-bay bar about 300 m north of the ramp: a ~1.3 ha area under 10 ft with an under-5-ft core, in 15–25 ft water (2004 contours, full pool).</desc><sym>Danger Area</sym><type>Hazard (rock, shallow, snag)</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.6968" lon="-116.92"><name>Rodkey Access</name><cmt>Rodkey Drive shore access (Kootenai County)</cmt><desc>Park / beach — 10-ft public pathway to the north bank — carry-in access only. Closed 10 p.m.–5 a.m. (KCC 6.2.122(B)).</desc><sym>Park</sym><type>Park / beach</type></wpt>
<wpt lat="47.6958" lon="-116.917"><name>Mile 7 zone?</name><cmt>&quot;Mile 7&quot; no-wake channel — location to confirm</cmt><desc>Other — KCC 6.2.122(A)(1)(c) designates &quot;the channel between the shoreline and the island and wetlands area at mile 7 on the south side&quot; as no-wake. Counted from the lake, mile 7 falls near Greensferry Bay, which has a south-side island — the likeliest match, but unconfirmed. Not drawn as a zone until HLWID or the county confirms.</desc><sym>Waypoint</sym><type>Other</type></wpt>
